WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.077 --> 00:00:01.282
- When the waiter comes back,

00:00:01.282 --> 00:00:03.167
just ask him to slip his
number on the napkin.

00:00:03.167 --> 00:00:05.738
- Um, any chance you could
just write your number

00:00:05.738 --> 00:00:08.364
down on like, a receipt
or a napkin or something?

00:00:08.364 --> 00:00:11.183
- [Waiter] Yeah, could we
leave it at a "we'll see?"

00:00:11.183 --> 00:00:12.399
(rusty hinge squeak)

00:00:12.399 --> 00:00:15.069
(jazz trumpet music)

00:00:15.069 --> 00:00:16.386
- We did a video together

00:00:16.386 --> 00:00:20.593
where we were handcuffed
to each other for 24 hours.

00:00:20.593 --> 00:00:22.288
It wasn't as terrible as I expected.

00:00:22.288 --> 00:00:23.698
- You might not have
thought it was as bad,

00:00:23.698 --> 00:00:25.637
my hand, when I got burned--

00:00:25.637 --> 00:00:27.513
(fire alarm siren)

00:00:27.513 --> 00:00:29.760
- Yeah you did get burned
while we were trying to cook.

00:00:29.760 --> 00:00:32.496
The girl I picked for
Will to go on a date with,

00:00:32.496 --> 00:00:33.627
I'm very proud of myself.

00:00:33.627 --> 00:00:35.886
I feel like Cupid here because I think

00:00:35.886 --> 00:00:37.814
that this is going to be
a match made in heaven.

00:00:37.814 --> 00:00:41.237
The twist here is that we're
going to have an ear piece

00:00:41.237 --> 00:00:43.902
telling each other exactly
what to say and what to do.

00:00:43.902 --> 00:00:46.562
I feel like I'm gonna be
so tempted to just like,

00:00:46.562 --> 00:00:48.122
completely sabotage the whole thing

00:00:48.122 --> 00:00:50.019
just for my own personal entertainment.

00:00:50.019 --> 00:00:51.190
(laughs)

00:00:51.190 --> 00:00:53.206
Pinky promise me right now you're gonna do

00:00:53.206 --> 00:00:54.665
exactly what I tell you to do

00:00:54.665 --> 00:00:56.500
and say what I'm gonna tell you to say.

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.313
- I will do exactly what you tell me to do

00:00:58.313 --> 00:00:59.932
and I will say exactly
what you tell me to say.

00:00:59.932 --> 00:01:00.765
- Okay.

00:01:00.765 --> 00:01:01.611
- [Juliana] Nice to meet you!

00:01:01.611 --> 00:01:04.559
- [Will] Nice to meet you too.

00:01:04.559 --> 00:01:07.056
- I have so much power
in my hands right now.

00:01:07.056 --> 00:01:08.280
- So where do you live?

00:01:08.280 --> 00:01:10.320
- I live in the Valley.

00:01:10.320 --> 00:01:12.023
But I'm originally from Texas.

00:01:12.023 --> 00:01:13.664
- I'm from Charlotte, North Carolina.

00:01:13.664 --> 00:01:14.622
- Is it cold there?

00:01:14.622 --> 00:01:16.299
- It does get cold.

00:01:16.299 --> 00:01:18.095
If it snows two inches,
the town shuts down.

00:01:18.095 --> 00:01:19.146
- Tell her that you're from the South

00:01:19.146 --> 00:01:20.545
so you're kind of afraid of the snow.

00:01:20.545 --> 00:01:23.364
- I'm from the South, so I'm
a little bit afraid of snow,

00:01:23.364 --> 00:01:24.924
cause people from the
South can't really drive.

00:01:24.924 --> 00:01:25.903
- They can't drive in it at all.

00:01:25.903 --> 00:01:26.994
- No.
The second it snows,

00:01:26.994 --> 00:01:27.920
like, people freak out.

00:01:27.920 --> 00:01:28.753
- What'd you move here for?

00:01:28.753 --> 00:01:30.898
- I moved here because I had a new job

00:01:30.898 --> 00:01:33.024
and I wanted to put
myself in an environment

00:01:33.024 --> 00:01:34.355
that would make me grow.

00:01:34.355 --> 00:01:36.001
- Ask her why she moved to L.A..

00:01:36.001 --> 00:01:37.608
- Why did you move here?

00:01:37.608 --> 00:01:38.490
- I do stand-up comedy.

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.653
- What's, like, your style of--

00:01:40.653 --> 00:01:43.633
- Lately it's been like,
literally like, dad jokes.

00:01:43.633 --> 00:01:45.498
- Ask her for her best dad joke.

00:01:45.498 --> 00:01:46.834
- Tell me your best dad joke.

00:01:46.834 --> 00:01:47.894
- Oh my gosh.

00:01:47.894 --> 00:01:48.727
(laughs)

00:01:48.727 --> 00:01:49.560
Nobody's gonna laugh.

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:50.393
Okay.

00:01:50.393 --> 00:01:51.234
(clears throat)

00:01:51.234 --> 00:01:53.133
Saw a cute homeless guy the other day.

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:55.307
Guess you could call
me a homeless romantic.

00:01:55.307 --> 00:01:57.045
(laughing)

00:01:57.045 --> 00:01:59.833
- Now tell her you want
to tell her a dad joke.

00:01:59.833 --> 00:02:01.639
- I'm gonna tell you a dad joke.

00:02:01.639 --> 00:02:04.214
- Say, what did the father chimney--

00:02:04.214 --> 00:02:06.297
- Say to the son chimney?

00:02:07.339 --> 00:02:08.626
- I know this one.

00:02:08.626 --> 00:02:10.303
But I don't remember it.

00:02:10.303 --> 00:02:11.136
Go.
Go go go.

00:02:11.136 --> 00:02:11.969
Say it.

00:02:11.969 --> 00:02:13.150
- No, ask her what the punch line is.

00:02:13.150 --> 00:02:14.566
- What do you think
like, the punch line is?

00:02:14.566 --> 00:02:15.741
- Wait, say it again?

00:02:15.741 --> 00:02:18.633
- Just tell her, you're
too young to smoke!

00:02:18.633 --> 00:02:20.610
- You're too young to smoke!

00:02:20.610 --> 00:02:22.265
- Oh okay, I get it.

00:02:22.265 --> 00:02:23.308
- It's the worst joke ever, I know.

00:02:23.308 --> 00:02:25.493
- It's a dad joke, cause it's about a dad.

00:02:25.493 --> 00:02:26.921
- Ask her what she was like growing up.

00:02:26.921 --> 00:02:28.597
- So what were you like
when you were growing up?

00:02:28.597 --> 00:02:29.430
- What I am today, just like

00:02:29.430 --> 00:02:30.263
(makes staccato energetic noises)

00:02:30.263 --> 00:02:31.096
- Yeah.
- You know?

00:02:31.096 --> 00:02:31.929
- Kind of a lot.

00:02:31.929 --> 00:02:33.948
- Yeah, like a lot.

00:02:33.948 --> 00:02:35.157
- Will, you just called her a lot!

00:02:35.157 --> 00:02:36.271
Take back that statement.

00:02:36.271 --> 00:02:38.581
- I didn't mean to like offend
you by saying you're a lot.

00:02:38.581 --> 00:02:39.572
- No it didn't.
I love it.

00:02:39.572 --> 00:02:40.538
That's like a compliment.

00:02:40.538 --> 00:02:42.227
- Say how much you love her personality.

00:02:42.227 --> 00:02:44.656
- I'm a lot too, so I mean-

00:02:44.656 --> 00:02:45.680
- Good.
- We could be a lot together.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:47.250
- Well it's better than being boring.

00:02:47.250 --> 00:02:48.171
- Oh wait, waiter's back.

00:02:48.171 --> 00:02:50.179
- Yeah, we'll take a quick look.

00:02:50.179 --> 00:02:51.804
- The waiter's hot.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.233
Set me up with the waiter.
(laughs)

00:02:53.233 --> 00:02:55.440
- Okay, so I'm gonna have the Kale Caesar.

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:56.465
- No tomatoes.

00:02:56.465 --> 00:02:57.298
- No tomatoes.

00:02:57.298 --> 00:03:00.084
- Say the reason why is
because I recently listened

00:03:00.084 --> 00:03:02.825
to a podcast with a evolutionary biologist

00:03:02.825 --> 00:03:05.594
and he said tomatoes are
indigenously poisonous

00:03:05.594 --> 00:03:06.427
to humans.

00:03:06.427 --> 00:03:07.260
Most people don't know.

00:03:07.260 --> 00:03:09.527
- So I actually don't
want tomatoes in my meal

00:03:09.527 --> 00:03:11.357
because I listened to a podcast recently,

00:03:11.357 --> 00:03:15.524
that says that um, tomatoes
are indigenously contagious-

00:03:16.692 --> 00:03:17.525
- Poisonous.

00:03:17.525 --> 00:03:18.358
Not contagious.

00:03:18.358 --> 00:03:19.191
- Poisonous!

00:03:19.191 --> 00:03:20.157
To humans.

00:03:20.157 --> 00:03:21.290
- Peanuts too!

00:03:21.290 --> 00:03:22.193
- Peanuts too!

00:03:22.193 --> 00:03:23.300
- You sound so L.A..

00:03:23.300 --> 00:03:24.364
- No tomatoes for me.

00:03:24.364 --> 00:03:26.377
- Everybody in L.A. is
like, this is bad for you,

00:03:26.377 --> 00:03:27.842
don't eat it, it's gonna kill you.

00:03:27.842 --> 00:03:29.722
That's you.
- I mean, what else can I say?

00:03:29.722 --> 00:03:31.005
- I'm out.
No I'm just kidding.

00:03:31.005 --> 00:03:31.838
(laughs)

00:03:31.838 --> 00:03:32.671
- Ah, look at this.

00:03:32.671 --> 00:03:33.887
- [Waiter] Here ya are.

00:03:33.887 --> 00:03:34.720
Almost had those mixed up.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:35.699
- Oh perfect, thank you.

00:03:35.699 --> 00:03:36.965
- She wants tomatoes.

00:03:36.965 --> 00:03:38.226
- Oh, looks good!

00:03:38.226 --> 00:03:39.176
Thank you.

00:03:39.176 --> 00:03:40.009
- Thank you.

00:03:40.009 --> 00:03:42.251
- So you got bread and tomatoes.

00:03:42.251 --> 00:03:43.249
- I didn't know it came with bread.

00:03:43.249 --> 00:03:45.358
Am I breaking some L.A. rule?

00:03:45.358 --> 00:03:47.421
- Yeah, you're so not L.A..

00:03:47.421 --> 00:03:48.582
- What is it called again?

00:03:48.582 --> 00:03:49.609
- That's um--

00:03:49.609 --> 00:03:51.095
- It's what you put on
your eyes, with, uh...

00:03:51.095 --> 00:03:52.355
- Yeah, that's a cucumber.

00:03:52.355 --> 00:03:53.188
- Cucumber!

00:03:53.188 --> 00:03:54.021
Do you like cucumbers?

00:03:54.021 --> 00:03:55.104
- I do like--

00:03:57.045 --> 00:03:58.502
- They're feeding each other!

00:03:58.502 --> 00:03:59.335
- That's good.

00:03:59.335 --> 00:04:01.221
- Things escalated quickly here.

00:04:01.221 --> 00:04:03.337
Ask her what she likes to do...

00:04:03.337 --> 00:04:04.170
- In your free time.

00:04:04.170 --> 00:04:06.134
- I like going to Mulholland Drive.

00:04:06.134 --> 00:04:06.967
- Where's that?

00:04:06.967 --> 00:04:08.598
- It's in between Studio
City and Hollywood.

00:04:08.598 --> 00:04:09.431
- Oh, okay.

00:04:09.431 --> 00:04:10.637
- Jim Carrey is the one
who inspired me to do

00:04:10.637 --> 00:04:11.651
stand-up comedy.

00:04:11.651 --> 00:04:14.395
But he used to go to the
top of Mulholland Drive

00:04:14.395 --> 00:04:15.730
and write himself, like a--

00:04:15.730 --> 00:04:17.360
- He would go to the top of the mountain--

00:04:17.360 --> 00:04:18.748
- And he'd write himself a check.

00:04:18.748 --> 00:04:19.602
Yeah.

00:04:19.602 --> 00:04:21.436
- Ask her if she believes
in the law of attraction,

00:04:21.436 --> 00:04:24.457
but say it with a seductive
twinkle in your eye.

00:04:24.457 --> 00:04:25.916
- Do you believe in the law of attraction?

00:04:25.916 --> 00:04:27.827
- How you manifest what you desire?

00:04:27.827 --> 00:04:30.259
- Yeah, like how you
manifest what you desire?

00:04:30.259 --> 00:04:31.225
- Oh, yeah.

00:04:31.225 --> 00:04:32.391
Okay, this is coming back.

00:04:32.391 --> 00:04:33.910
You know, you're so funny.

00:04:33.910 --> 00:04:35.713
Everybody in L.A. is about the universe!

00:04:35.713 --> 00:04:36.571
- Yeah.
- There's nothing wrong

00:04:36.571 --> 00:04:37.404
with that.

00:04:37.404 --> 00:04:38.237
- [Waiter] I don't mean to
interrupt, is everything

00:04:38.237 --> 00:04:39.070
tasting alright?

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:40.161
- Oh yeah, it's great.
- [Will] This is amazing.

00:04:40.161 --> 00:04:40.994
- Wait, Will!

00:04:40.994 --> 00:04:42.402
Ask the waiter for his number.

00:04:42.402 --> 00:04:43.860
- Uh, excuse me sir, actually-

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:45.322
- Tell him you're asking for a friend.

00:04:45.322 --> 00:04:49.287
- Is there any chance I
could get your phone number?

00:04:49.287 --> 00:04:50.803
- You're asking for a friend.

00:04:50.803 --> 00:04:52.655
- I don't personally want it, but...

00:04:52.655 --> 00:04:53.526
- [Waiter] Gotcha.

00:04:53.526 --> 00:04:54.359
Um...

00:04:54.359 --> 00:04:55.394
- He hasn't even asked for my number.

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:56.227
You're lucky.

00:04:56.227 --> 00:04:57.254
- Sounds like it's going well.

00:04:57.254 --> 00:04:58.087
- Yeah.

00:04:58.087 --> 00:04:58.920
(laughs)

00:04:58.920 --> 00:04:59.753
Alright.

00:04:59.753 --> 00:05:01.661
- Tell her sorry about that
I was asking for a friend.

00:05:01.661 --> 00:05:03.304
- You're just hilarious, honestly you are.

00:05:03.304 --> 00:05:04.277
- You're funny too.

00:05:04.277 --> 00:05:05.943
Thank you.
- I'm funny?

00:05:05.943 --> 00:05:07.293
- He's doing great.

00:05:07.293 --> 00:05:09.734
Ask her what she looks for in a partner.

00:05:09.734 --> 00:05:10.676
- Ooh, that's easy.

00:05:10.676 --> 00:05:11.509
Someone who's funny.

00:05:11.509 --> 00:05:12.610
- So, X on that.

00:05:12.610 --> 00:05:13.714
- No, I mean, you're...

00:05:13.714 --> 00:05:14.547
(laughs)

00:05:14.547 --> 00:05:16.316
- Someone who eats
dressing on their salad.

00:05:16.316 --> 00:05:17.149
Just kidding.

00:05:17.149 --> 00:05:17.982
(laughs)

00:05:17.982 --> 00:05:19.942
He's pissed about the salad.

00:05:19.942 --> 00:05:20.775
Muahahaha!

00:05:21.629 --> 00:05:23.580
Ask her how she thinks the date's going--

00:05:23.580 --> 00:05:24.413
- So far?

00:05:24.413 --> 00:05:25.446
- It's like a lot of fun.

00:05:25.446 --> 00:05:26.546
I haven't been on a date in a while.

00:05:26.546 --> 00:05:27.899
- So it's a lot of fun because
you haven't been on a date

00:05:27.899 --> 00:05:29.051
in a while, or it's actually a lot of fun?

00:05:29.051 --> 00:05:30.846
- In general, it's a great date.

00:05:30.846 --> 00:05:31.679
- Okay.

00:05:31.679 --> 00:05:33.045
- It's a great date!
Look at me.

00:05:33.045 --> 00:05:34.370
- I haven't been on a
date in a while either.

00:05:34.370 --> 00:05:35.203
- Really?

00:05:35.203 --> 00:05:37.736
- I'm taking all the credit for this.

00:05:37.736 --> 00:05:40.350
- Ask her if she'd like
to go on a second date.

00:05:40.350 --> 00:05:42.598
- I know I haven't been super
hilarious this whole date.

00:05:42.598 --> 00:05:44.323
and this has been like,
okay, and the wine--

00:05:44.323 --> 00:05:47.274
- He's discrediting his humor,

00:05:47.274 --> 00:05:48.873
which is discrediting my humor.

00:05:48.873 --> 00:05:49.939
- Would you wanna go on a second date?

00:05:49.939 --> 00:05:51.018
- Heck yeah!

00:05:51.018 --> 00:05:52.684
- Yeah?
- Where?

00:05:52.684 --> 00:05:53.517
- Where?

00:05:53.517 --> 00:05:54.909
Um, I'm not gonna tell you.

00:05:54.909 --> 00:05:55.742
- Ooh!

00:05:55.742 --> 00:05:56.575
I love surprises!

00:05:56.575 --> 00:05:57.408
- Yeah.

00:05:57.408 --> 00:05:59.766
- You totally t-ed me up
and you gave me all the ammo

00:05:59.766 --> 00:06:01.722
that I needed, and that's
why next time I go on a date

00:06:01.722 --> 00:06:03.397
I'm gonna put you in my ear again.

00:06:03.397 --> 00:06:06.558
- Okay, that will be 500 dollars please.

00:06:06.558 --> 00:06:10.045
This was fun, and I can walk away knowing

00:06:10.045 --> 00:06:14.156
that in karmic law, this
will come back around to me.

00:06:14.156 --> 00:06:16.573
(jazz music)

00:06:21.947 --> 00:06:24.158
- [Sky] So we'll set up
a second date for you,

00:06:24.158 --> 00:06:26.158
and 100 dollars an hour.

00:06:27.540 --> 00:06:28.373
Cheers to that.

